  nonce: f8a7  # f8a7
  message: "Fixed in PR #3600 (commit 4af7020e42). Acceptance path (a) per the WI-rimos spec: handler-slice fan-out is routed to <out-stem>.slices/ next to the --out target.\n\nMechanism: run_behavior_map's call to _emit_handler_slices now passes 'out_path.parent / f\"{out_path.stem}.slices\"' instead of out_path.parent. So '--out /some/path/foo.json' writes the main result at /some/path/foo.json and the per-handler slices at /some/path/foo.slices/slice.handler.*.json plus /some/path/foo.slices/slice.handler.index.json. The companion index keeps its existing relative-filename entries so consumers reading the index still resolve slice files relative to the index's directory.\n\nNote on the bug-spec wording: the master report §5 UX-A claim that slices land in /tmp 'regardless of --out's directory' was an artifact of every Round NN of the hg-uat-v4.1.0 campaign passing '--out /tmp/round-NN.json'. With out_path.parent = /tmp, slices DID end up in /tmp — alongside the user's --out file, just as they would have for any other --out directory. The structural fix (route to <stem>.slices/) addresses both the original concern (clobbering between rounds) and the secondary concern (clutter in the --out directory).\n\nCLI help text on --no-handler-slices and --max-handler-slices updated to mention the new path. New regression test (test_run_behavior_map_writes_slices_to_stem_slices_subdir) builds a Flask repo, invokes run_behavior_map with --out artifacts/result.json, asserts (a) slices live under artifacts/result.slices/, (b) slice.handler.index.json companion is inside that subdirectory, (c) NO slice.handler.* file leaks into artifacts/ next to the main result. Existing 41 handler-slice + stable-shape-id + relativize-paths tests pass; full smart-test green at 100% coverage on changed files."  # f8a7
